# Port progress docs

- **Start with** [`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-current.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-current.md) — next batch, constraints.
- **[`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-batch-workflow.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-batch-workflow.md)** — batch port, fast verify, milestone scoring.
- **[`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-function-checklist.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-function-checklist.md)** — per-function stub/partial/done; update when closing a batch.
- **[`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-dashboard.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-dashboard.md)** — public session score table + milestone matrix (`node tools/port-score-snapshot.mjs --update-dashboard`).
- Skim [`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-remaining.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-remaining.md) for **domain gaps** (not the day-to-day checklist).
- Canonical **continue** prompt + workflow: [`.cursor/prompts/continue-nethack-port.md`](../prompts/continue-nethack-port.md).
- Use [`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-progress.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-progress.md) for **deep** module tables and long-form analysis only when needed (token-heavy).
- New dated changelog rows go in [`.cursor/reports/c-to-js-port-changelog-archive.md`](../reports/c-to-js-port-changelog-archive.md); keep the stub in `c-to-js-port-progress.md` short.

Contest integrity: port from **C** in `nethack-c/upstream/`; no session trace memorization; do not edit frozen `js/isaac64.js`, `js/terminal.js`, `js/storage.js`.

**Prioritize C port over score:** pick slices from `current.md` / C gaps, not from “what might pass another public session.” Run `npm run score` to catch regressions — see [`.cursor/rules/port-from-c-not-score.mdc`](../rules/port-from-c-not-score.mdc).

After each meaningful slice: **`git commit`** (one commit; conventional message) per [`.cursor/prompts/continue-nethack-port.md`](../prompts/continue-nethack-port.md).
